  "behavior": [
    "Bounded stack allocations can flow as ordinary SSA addresses through pointer PHIs, selections, stores, casts and returns while retaining storage ownership and copy extents.",
    "Call preservation saves every live scalar and pair alias in caller-clobbered registers.",
    "Checked signed and unsigned add/subtract/multiply pairs support widths one through 32 with exact result and overflow semantics; unsigned word add/subtract remains supported.",
    "General boolean call results preserve their low ABI bit through pointer arguments, stack arguments and indirect calls.",
    "Zero extension from a truncated i32 accumulator clears stale upper RAX bits through the existing typed cast transaction.",
    "The unchanged pinned upstream Fibonacci program still executes all six assertions in ReleaseFast and ReleaseSmall, matching LLVM exit status, stdout and stderr."
  ],
